# Veloct is developed on Windows but its build inputs must hash identically anywhere.
# `handoff.md` §14.9 requires a historical release to rebuild reproducibly, and the content
# hash in `docs/spec/01-data-model.md` §3 is computed over normalised text. Normalising line
# endings in the repository is what keeps a clone on another machine from looking modified.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only binary artefacts must never be line-ending-normalised.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
*.crate binary

# Generated lockfiles are committed on purpose (a release freezes its lockfile hash) but should
# not clutter diffs or be merged by hand.
Cargo.lock -diff linguist-generated
site/package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
